# Changelog

## 0.2.0 — 2026-10-11

- Registrations that omit scope now support requesting read and write. Tokens
  still carry only locally approved authorization scopes; existing clients and
  explicitly read-only registrations remain unchanged.
- Corrected protected-resource discovery to advertise optional write scope while
  retaining read-only minimum authentication and existing read grants.

- Opt-in preview/commit tools with 16 fixed write operations: workouts,
  scheduling/removal, device push, manual activities, bounded FIT/TCX/GPX uploads,
  activity edits, strength sets and health measurements.
- Dated workout batches for calendars (not native Garmin Coach plans).
- Encrypted intent journals, expiry, duplicate protection and partial progress;
  no application-level mutation retries or read-cache reuse.
- Separate garmin:write grants; existing grants remain read-only.
- Workout template reads, validation tests and branch/PR/merge contribution flow.

## 0.1.0 — 2026-10-11

Initial public release:
- Seven bounded, read-only Garmin activity and training tools over MCP stdio.
- Interactive login and MFA; Windows DPAPI session encryption.
- Local Codex plugin and interpreter-aware Windows installer.
- Optional ngrok HTTPS access with OAuth, PKCE, local consent, refresh rotation
  and revocation. Owner verified access in ChatGPT on a phone.
- Offline tests and Windows/Linux CI; current ChatGPT callback-ID support.

Limits: unofficial Garmin API; personal single-owner remote service; PC must
stay online. Remote setup is tested on Windows. ChatGPT mobile availability
depends on the account and workspace.
